---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import SectionHero from "../../components/SectionHero.astro";
import contract from "../../data/lifecycle/resolved-roles.json";
const framework = contract.framework;
const domains = Object.fromEntries(framework.domains.map(d => [d.id, d.name]));
const profiles = {...contract.roles, ...Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(contract.available_domain_profiles).filter(([key]) => key !== "domain"))};
---
<Base title="Simulation roles and proficiency · Capability Matters" active="problems-to-prototypes">
 <meta slot="head" name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
 <SectionHero eyebrow="Lifecycle role contract" title="Inherit responsibilities. Demonstrate proficiency."
 claim="A role profile defines a bounded contribution to the project. A parent supplies shared duties; a specialist or domain profile adds context and requested proficiency. Inheritance supplies no performance evidence."
 question="What work would justify the claim that this role can perform in this context?" />
 <section class="container roles">
  <p><a href="/agentic-le/">Project lifecycle</a> · <a href="/agentic-le/replay/">Replay the exemplar</a> · <a href="/agentic-le/roles.json">Download the resolved role contract</a></p>
  <p><strong>Registry {contract.registry_version}; framework {contract.framework_version}.</strong> The domain names come from Capability Matters’ public LENS framework. These proficiency descriptors are proposed simulation expectations, not an adopted credentialing standard or a statement of human or model proficiency.</p>
  <h2>Requested contribution levels</h2>
  <div class="levels">{Object.entries(framework.proficiencies).map(([id, level]) => <article><h3>{level.name}</h3><p>{level.expectation}</p><p><strong>Evidence needed to review performance:</strong></p><ul>{level.evidence_required.map(item => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul></article>)}</div>
  <h2>Resolved role profiles</h2>
  <p>Shared contributor → specialist → domain specialization is a composition path, not an automatic promotion. Duties accumulate; child targets replace the parent target for the same domain. Human approval boundaries remain in code and do not expand through role inheritance.</p>
  {Object.entries(profiles).map(([id, profile]) => <article id={id} class="profile"><h3>{profile.name}</h3><p class="lineage">{profile.lineage.join(" → ")}</p><p>{profile.competency}</p><details><summary>Inherited and specialized duties</summary><ul>{profile.duties.map(duty => <li>{duty}</li>)}</ul></details><table><caption>Requested simulation proficiency</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">LENS domain</th><th scope="col">Target contribution</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.entries(profile.proficiency_targets).map(([domain, target]) => <tr><th scope="row">{domain}: {domains[domain]}</th><td>{framework.proficiencies[target].name}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><p class="unknown"><strong>Demonstrated proficiency:</strong> unverified. Review context-specific task performance, support conditions, evidence coverage and transfer before making a capability claim.</p></article>)}
  <h2>Adding a domain or future competency framework</h2><p>Extend an existing concrete profile in the versioned registry, name the domain assumptions and required practitioner validation, then test resolution. Future runs store the exact resolved profiles and framework hashes. A new authoritative framework can be added with source and version identifiers, an explicit crosswalk and separately reviewed proficiency evidence; a name match or successful model response does not establish equivalence.</p>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/tree/main/src/data/lifecycle">Versioned registry source</a> · <a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/blob/main/docs/lifecycle/ROLES.md">Role contract</a> · <a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/blob/main/docs/lifecycle/PROFICIENCY.md">Evidence and proficiency rules</a></p>
 </section>
</Base>
<style>.roles{padding-top:2rem;padding-bottom:3rem}.levels{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem}article{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1.2rem;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:1.4rem}h3{margin-top:0}.lineage{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);overflow-wrap:anywhere}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:1rem;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.88rem}caption{text-align:left;font-weight:700;padding:.6rem 0}th,td{text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.6rem}.unknown{background:var(--tint);padding:.9rem;font-size:.9rem}@media(max-width:720px){.levels{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
